y, | and a query's { raw; it used to fail \"Invalid redirect URI\". A Location java.net.URI accepts is followed as before. DESIGN.md names both. ApacheHttpClientRawTargetTest. Gate: karate-core 3115 tests (3 skipped), 0 failures; karate-js 1964.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"moq-dev/moq","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:14:02Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"ce5977241636293f5f8dfb338335a113830503ba","github_link":"https://github.com/moq-dev/moq/commit/ce5977241636293f5f8dfb338335a113830503ba","commit_subject":"feat: one UDP port for QUIC and the WebRTC media path (#7095)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"jondgoodwin/cone","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:51Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"b6e05cdd3d7b3982dd723606c6ad21e585653dea","github_link":"https://github.com/jondgoodwin/cone/commit/b6e05cdd3d7b3982dd723606c6ad21e585653dea","commit_subject":"Root the stable sort's merge buffer while the merge runs (Bug 33)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"pymedphys/pymedphys","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:32Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"4a4e3c258181f19e62808b69fa58e6cda4b50839","github_link":"https://github.com/pymedphys/pymedphys/commit/4a4e3c258181f19e62808b69fa58e6cda4b50839","commit_subject":"Give the narrow-extras unit-test jobs a 60-minute limit","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:28Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"ba4aef8bd87aafdfe620f375e45bdd5a8176d3cb","github_link":"https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/commit/ba4aef8bd87aafdfe620f375e45bdd5a8176d3cb","commit_subject":"hic_structural_variants: cut the EBF1 compartments section","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:05Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"2cdac5a86cc4c7adc589645849c48748e08365d0","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/2cdac5a86cc4c7adc589645849c48748e08365d0","commit_subject":"Client: a new app falls back to the old protocol on a server before 15 (owner, 2026-11-01). A 9.0.859 server answers HTTP 15 with a 401, which the app cannot tell from a refused proof, so its hello tries the legacy HTTP once - no proof, and 8 until the hello agrees on a version, then that one below 15 - unless that server took 15 before in this process: no 401 talks the app down from the proof there. Each server's way is remembered per endpoint and farm; one that took only the legacy way is asked that way first, and 15 again once it refuses that. A legacy session offers no WebSocket masking, so no padding, and runs no QUIC clock recovery. Servers and apps update in either order now; protocol-15.md, the release checklist and CHANGELOG.Server say so. ServerHost's newest HTTP version is settable for tests, where 14 makes a server before 15","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:05Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"bb6dbf7cd0999d0e73f7dffe3cf01be0eac832e1","github_link":"https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/commit/bb6dbf7cd0999d0e73f7dffe3cf01be0eac832e1","commit_subject":"Variant display: one hover slot; one per-region map over the payload","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:03Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"716295a40caaf548ba54fbc2cc0fad27fde19575","github_link":"https://github.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/716295a40caaf548ba54fbc2cc0fad27fde19575","commit_subject":"fix(engine): a match shows as many cards as real football","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:13:00Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"4a147ca1516a5095117a2af7b5cda1faec1c9995","github_link":"https://github.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/4a147ca1516a5095117a2af7b5cda1faec1c9995","commit_subject":"test(engine): a match shows as many cards as real football","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:1